{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790327958,"nonce":"1sHhoHcRrxX9EuNpkll2LXrP/Jc=","title":"Call-site caches lose getter sites: never recorded from compiled code, cleared by unrelated installs","message":"bench/method_call.wren makes 2M calls; WLIFT_TIER_STATS=1 at 1702fc8\nshows 1,055,059 of them going through the generic wren_call helper,\n914,096 of those answered by the runtime's trivial-getter shortcut:\n`ntoggle.activate.value` in the second loop never gets its `.value`\nloaded inline, in any compile of the module body.\n\nTwo defects, found with WLIFT_TRACE_JIT_IC / WLIFT_INLINE_TRACE and a\nbacktrace on every overwrite of a kind-5 entry:\n\n1. try_dispatch_call_noframe_fast, the first stop for every call from\n   compiled code, answers a trivial getter or setter on a method-cache\n   hit and returns without recording the call site. Only the first\n   call of a (class, method) pair misses the method cache and takes\n   the full path that records the site; every other site answered by\n   the shortcut stays empty, and each recompile leaves it generic. In\n   method_call one of the ten `.value` sites of the second loop was\n   recorded (the cache-missing one), nine never.\n\n2. invalidate_ic_entries_for(N), run at every install of function N,\n   clears every entry whose func_id == N. For kind 5 func_id is the\n   field index, for kind 8 a host context, for kinds 4 and 9 zero; so\n   installing function N also clears the getter entries of field N,\n   and installing FuncId(0) (usually a module body) clears every\n   native and List entry. In method_call each install of the module\n   body wiped the `.value` getter entries (field 0) that had been\n   recorded, so the LLVM compile saw none.\n\nFix: record the site on the shortcut as the full path would (only when\nit has not seen this class, so the steady state costs nothing more),\nand clear only entries whose func_id names a function (kinds 1, 2, 3,\n6, 7).","files":null}]}